 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Relaxed standing, sitting, lying supine, prone and lateral; loads measured about 100 days after anterior interbody fusion; video-synchronised telemetry.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Model the patient (Table 1: sex, age, height, weight, bridged vertebra/fixator levels) in each body position: standing, sitting (stool), lying supine, prone, lateral",
   "No external load; relaxed posture",
   "Output the axial force in the bisegmental fixator rods (or, for whole-spine models, the segment compression at the bridged level) for each position",
   "A whole-spine MSK model outputs total segment loads, not the fixator share; fixator loads depend strongly on surgical procedure (distraction/compression, bridged level, interbody fusion) - compare only trends/relative values unless the model includes the bisegmental fixator and its load sharing; robust targets: standing > lying, sitting <= standing"
  ],
